<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hubal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hubal was a god worshipped in pre-Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, whose statue of red stone with a golden hand stood inside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a>. Divination arrows were cast before it to settle disputes and decisions. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> invoked him in their wars against Muhammad, and the image was destroyed when the Muslims took Mecca in 630.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hubal.jpg" alt="Hubal" width="212" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AimanAbir18plus · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubal,_pre-Islamic_Arabian_god.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
